      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe this should also come with parameter naming for convenience, adding the ability to choose whether to use maximum, minimum, or average for the global Stretch and Angle values, and to list them all out independently as `_1_IsGrabbed` `_2_IsGrabbed` etc for convenience and usage in animators, as well as syncing physbone events. this should also allow (ideally) some form of “tethering” i.e. when used in skirts to allow for one chain to affect/pull another in the same component like regular cloth does (see magica cloth unity for example)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-07T23:53:02.666Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In some cases (for example, with skirts or hair bones), you want to apply the same physbone configuration for multiple related bone chains. While you could enable PhysBones for a common root, this has side effects - in particular, some folks are asking for the root to have physics, which in this case would be undesirable. It would be cleaner to be able to simply specify multiple root transforms, rather than having to duplicate the component.\nSuggested (in japanese) at https://twitter.com/pre287/status/1500956967354847232",
